  "summary": [
    "B27 distant-paths. Seven exact sources become aliases of two public contracts of `GTBase.distant_paths`: the raw relation `pairwise_distant_seqs d paths` (X39, X116, X26 pairwise relations and X146's A-named one; every two unequal sequence values of the supplied list have the closed `d.-1` `set_ball` around one support missing the other) and `has_k_distant_set_paths d k X Y` (X39, X116, X26 wrappers: exact size k, `uniq`, B5 `seq_set_path` entries). X26's two sources are conversions; X39 / X116 / X146 drop a redundant disjointness conjunct through the unconditional `pairwise_distant_seqsP` and `has_k_distant_set_pathsP`. No guard, argument or carrier changes.",
    "",
    "Corners, in the module and the public-only client base/theories/examples/distant_paths.v: empty host and empty or singleton families; equal raw duplicates accepted by the relation but never a `uniq` witness; d = 0 and d = 1 coincide; k = 0 always and k = 1 iff one X-Y path, a one-vertex path for overlapping endpoints; monotone in d and under restriction; K_2's endpoints are distant for d = 1 but not 2; two isolated vertices are distant for every d.",
    "",
    "Frozen at 058da18 with every guard: X146's A-path existence chain (distinct endpoints, internal avoidance kept) and five complete current rows, X39 ball separator, cross-module X40 distance 2 (partial), X116 bounded separator, X146 coarse Gallai and Packing X26 bounded-degree Menger (d = 0 kept), each by a pointwise transport (X26 by conversion). A22's complete X39, X40, X116, X146 and X26 Originals (raw balls, B1 supports, B5 paths, B5 / B26 separators) are reused with A22's certificates: ten whole iff. Twenty-seven earlier frozen copies of the sources and chain (B1 9e03072, B5 fbf33a0, A22 1b8126b / 9e03072) are bound as historical objects; B5's three Legacy wrappers, which keep the live raw relation, are documented partial snapshots.",
    "",
    "Old certificates keep every statement and frozen body; proofs that reached the live helpers by conversion now use the public bridges (dated comments). Routes: X39, X40, X116, X146 (graph-theory-misc) and X26 (packing-theory); no Digraph source. X113's distant cycles (radius d) stay a separate family."
  ],
